  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_penistone_cb0">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>probably penistones, a kind of coarse woollen cloth formerly used for garments, linings, etc. from the name of a small town in the West Riding of Yorkshire, where the cloth so named was made (OED penistone) | a kind of coarse woollen cloth formerly used for garments, linings, etc. from the name of a small town in the West Riding of Yorkshire, where the cloth so named was made (OED penistone), reckoned four to the cloth of assize unfrised, two to the cloth of assize frised) (Jenks 138) | a kind of coarse woollen cloth formerly used for garments, linings, etc. from the name of a small town in the West Riding of Yorkshire, where the cloth so named was made (OED penistone), reckoned four to the cloth of assize unfrised, two to the cloth of assize frised (Jenks 2024, p. 124) | (pennystone whightes) an English woollen | a kind of English woollen, reckoned at two to a cloth of assize</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
